-- One-time seed: a baseline "country snapshot" (region, income group,
-- capital, population, GDP) for every country this app's globe can select
-- (frontend/src/lib/worldCountries.ts), not just the ~33 this app has U.S.
-- trade-policy data for. Source: the World Bank's free, keyless country API
-- (api.worldbank.org/v2/country/{code} for region/income/capital;
-- .../indicator/SP.POP.TOTL and NY.GDP.MKTP.CD with mrnev=1 for the most
-- recent non-empty population/GDP figures). Fetched once and checked in here
-- as a dated snapshot -- not re-fetched live on every click, same philosophy
-- as pulseBlocs.ts's static bloc membership and migration 0018's NATO
-- defense-spending figures. Re-verify by hand and re-seed periodically
-- (population/GDP are annual figures anyway, not daily-moving data).
--
-- Real, honest gaps, not bugs:
--   - Four codes worldCountries.ts tracks have no row here because the World
--     Bank itself has no entry for them: Taiwan (TW -- a political-
--     recognition decision on the World Bank's part, not this app's),
--     Falkland Islands (FK), French Southern and Antarctic Lands (TF), and
--     Western Sahara (EH) -- the latter three are small/uninhabited or
--     disputed territories the World Bank simply doesn't classify as member
--     economies. No figure is fabricated for any of them.
--   - "Government type" (e.g. "federal republic", "constitutional monarchy")
--     was in this feature's original plan, but no confirmed free, keyless,
--     bulk-structured source for it was found live (the World Bank's own
--     country metadata has no such field; CIA World Factbook has one but
--     publishes it only as HTML pages, not a bulk API) -- left out rather
--     than guessed. "Political" context for a country without U.S. trade
--     action history still comes from its real bloc memberships
--     (pulseBlocs.ts) and this table's region/capital.
--
-- Fetched 2026-10-02. population/GDP are each that country's own most recent
-- available year per the World Bank (mostly 2025, some countries lag).
CREATE TABLE country_snapshot (
  country_code     TEXT PRIMARY KEY,   -- ISO 3166-1 alpha-2
  region            TEXT NOT NULL,      -- World Bank region grouping
  income_level      TEXT NOT NULL,     -- World Bank income classification
  capital_city      TEXT,              -- NULL where the World Bank has none on file
  population        INTEGER,           -- NULL where unavailable
  population_year   TEXT,
  gdp_usd           REAL,              -- current US$, NULL where unavailable
  gdp_year          TEXT,
  source_url        TEXT NOT NULL,
  source_tier       INTEGER NOT NULL,
  last_updated      TEXT NOT NULL
);

